From 49de274e80d57e03798b77e92de0046ae1da79a2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: YBS Ai <ybs-ai@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 07:56:19 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix: bundle server assets reliably and make extraction
 recoverable

- MainActivity: only create .extracted_v1 after verifying
  out/server-main.js; a missing/failed extraction now removes its
  output so Retry re-extracts instead of failing forever on a stale
  marker. copyAssetFolder() returns the copied file count and an
  empty APK asset bundle fails with an actionable message.
- fetch-openvscode-assets.sh: tar --no-same-owner (tar aborted on
  uid/gid restore before copying assets when run as another user),
  verify staged bundle (server-main.js + >1000 files), preserve the
  tracked assets/vscode/.gitkeep.
- build-apk.sh: always (re)stage server assets and verify them
  before flutter pub get / flutter build apk, so a build fails
  loudly instead of producing an APK that only fails on the tablet.
- CI: explicit fetch + verify step before the APK build.
- verify-source.sh: regression checks for the above.
- README/TODO: document that the editor starts without the Linux
  glibc native modules (spdlog load is caught; verified the staged
  v1.109.5 server serves HTTP 200 on a Linux host), while the
  integrated terminal (node-pty) and native file watcher still need
  an Android Bionic rebuild.
